CORRECTED CLAIM: a 13-term AP is TIGHT iff a = d (i.e. it is a dilate
of {1,...,13}).  Dilation invariance (THM-1075) forces this.
    a=d cases:
      a=d=1: [1, 2, 3]...  uncovered = 0.00000000   (= 1*{1..13})
