    MINIMUM OVER PRIMITIVE (gcd=1) 13-TERM APs, scanning a,d <= 16:
      min = 0.00000000 at a=1, d=1
      primitive tight APs found: [(1, 1)]

  => among PRIMITIVE APs the only tight one is a=d=1, i.e. {1,...,13};
     every other primitive AP has a strictly positive margin, and the
     non-primitive tight cases are exactly its dilates k*{1,...,13}.
